{"text": "eo)\n\n}\n\nRESEARCH LABORATORY FTR, MARCH 1973 14.\n\n30. Interaction of Smoke with Cysteine\n\n1. Summary\n\nAlthough the work is temporarily suspended while waiting for\nnew laboratory space, it should be recalled that the purpose\nof this project is to identify those smoke constituents which\ncan react with cysteine.\n\n2. Glossary\n\n~ cysteine\nHg - CH - COOH :\n\\ { + is an amino acid which is essential for any\nSH NH\n\nliving organism, It plays 2 key role in protein structures\n(-S ~ 8 - bridging), as functional unit in many enzymes and\nas main protective agent in cell metabolism. It is the latter\nfunction that makes it interesting from the tobacco chemist's\npoint of view. Cysteine has been shown to protect certain\ncell functions against inhibition by smoke (see literature at\nthe end of the chapter). .\n\n- ISH (Index SH)\n\nThis expression was chosen for practical reasons. It indicates\nsimply the amount of free SH-groups blockga by smoke in an\nexperiment under defined smoking conditions (see Monthly Report,\nJanuary 1972).\n\n3. Objectives ,\n\nTo clear up the reaction mechanism of tobacco smoke with\ncysteine (separation and identification of the reaction\nproducts). By knowing the reaction products of smoke\ncomponents with cysteine, the nature of these can be\nstablished. This information is necessary for the project\n\"Product Research\" for future product modification in order\nto meet advanced product specifications.\n\nO16z9zt0Sz", "words": [{"text": "eo)", "x0": 16, "y0": 354, "x1": 38, "y1": 374, "conf": 0.0}, {"text": "}", "x0": 43, "y0": 395, "x1": 47, "y1": 410, "conf": 2.0}, {"text": "RESEARCH", "x0": 100, "y0": 56, "x1": 168, "y1": 68, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "LABORATORY", "x0": 178, "y0": 57, "x1": 267, "y1": 65, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "FTR,", "x0": 277, "y0": 57, "x1": 310, "y1": 68, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "MARCH", "x0": 320, "y0": 47, "x1": 365, "y1": 72, "conf": 44.0}, {"text": "1973", "x0": 373, "y0": 52, "x1": 409, "y